From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: count stations from the live provider snapshot

The AP Metrics report serializes station records from client_stats_map. It
must derive its count from that same authoritative live snapshot. The
event-backed associated_devices_map can be empty when a station associated
before OneWifi started, and can retain inactive history after a roam.

The current upstream source added locking around associated_devices_map.
Since the report does not serialize that map, remove that access and its lock
rather than protecting and counting an unrelated data source. Count
client_stats_map and publish the same count in both report fields.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
index 7baff84..bc355e9 100644
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -2000,26 +2000,14 @@ static int ap_report_push_cb(em_ap_report_callback_arg_t *args)
 
             //index cannot be vap index below right for cache retrieval, have to search in the all cache for each vaps and check vap index
             ap_metrics = &em_ap_metrics_report_cache.radio_report[radio_index].ap_data[cache_vap_index].ap_metrics;
-            rdk_wifi_vap_info_t *rdk_vap_info = &wifi_mgr->radio_config[radio_index].vaps.rdk_vap_array[j];
-            pthread_mutex_t *assoc_lock = rdk_vap_info->associated_devices_lock;
-
-            if (assoc_lock != NULL) {
-                pthread_mutex_lock(assoc_lock);
-            }
-
-            if (rdk_vap_info->associated_devices_map == NULL) {
-                wifi_util_dbg_print(WIFI_EM,
-                    "%s:%d: associated_devices_map is NULL for radio_index %d and vap_index %d\n",
-                    __func__, __LINE__, radio_index, rdk_vap_info->vap_index);
-                ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas = 0;
-            } else {
-                ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas = hash_map_count(rdk_vap_info->associated_devices_map);
-            }
-
-            if (assoc_lock != NULL) {
-                pthread_mutex_unlock(assoc_lock);
-            }
-            vap_report->sta_cnt = ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas;
+            /* Serialize and count the same authoritative live snapshot. The
+             * event-backed associated_devices_map can miss a station which
+             * associated before OneWifi started, while client_stats_map is
+             * refreshed by the current HAL provider response. */
+            vap_report->sta_cnt = hash_map_count(
+                em_ap_metrics_report_cache.radio_report[radio_index]
+                    .ap_data[cache_vap_index].client_stats_map);
+            ap_metrics->num_of_assoc_stas = vap_report->sta_cnt;
             memcpy(ap_metrics->bssid, vap_info->u.bss_info.bssid, sizeof(bssid_t));
             memcpy(&vap_report->vap_metrics, ap_metrics, sizeof(ap_metrics_t));
             to_mac_str(vap_info->u.bss_info.bssid, bss_str);

